intent: >
  Add the infra/ topic (tflint/tfsec/trivy/terraform-docs/packer/pre-commit/ansible)
  the repo audit found in heavy use, owned per docs/package-matrix.md.
slice: "2D/6"
kind: feature
behavior_change: additive
reversibility: reversible
scope:
  declared:
    - infra/install.sh
    - homebrew/Brewfile
    - script/packages/ubuntu.sh
  actual:
    - infra/install.sh
    - homebrew/Brewfile
    - script/packages/ubuntu.sh
  drift: []
proof:
  tests_run: "zsh -n infra/install.sh; bash -n + shellcheck script/packages/ubuntu.sh; brew info on the new formulae"
  result: green
  failing: 0
tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    No suite; zsh -n on infra/install.sh, shellcheck clean on ubuntu.sh. Verified
    pre-commit/tfsec/trivy/terraform-docs/ansible/packer are valid core formulae;
    tflint needs the terraform-linters/tap (Brewfile now taps it + uses the
    qualified name). infra/install.sh's Linux path was NOT executed (needs apt) —
    real run is the Ubuntu VM step.
lint:
  run: "shellcheck script/packages/ubuntu.sh"
  result: clean
  count: 0
verification:
  tested:
    - "infra/install.sh passes zsh -n; ubuntu.sh shellcheck clean"
    - "6 infra formulae valid in homebrew/core; tflint resolved via terraform-linters/tap"
  manual:
    - "Linux install paths (curl|bash scripts, terraform-docs tarball, pipx) reviewed only, not run"
assumptions:
  - "tflint/tfsec/trivy official install scripts are current and install to /usr/local/bin"
  - "terraform-docs v0.19.0 release tarball exists for linux-amd64 and linux-arm64"
  - "ansible 2.18.7 installs cleanly via pipx on the managed Python"
  - "terraform-linters/tap is the correct Homebrew tap for tflint (confirmed by brew's own error message)"
specifications:
  - "packer is the only infra tool installed via the HashiCorp apt repo (in ubuntu.sh); the rest live in infra/install.sh"
  - "Both tfsec and trivy are installed (migration window)"
  - "pre-commit + ansible install via pipx on Linux (from python/install.sh), via Homebrew on macOS"
deviations_from_plan: none
trade_offs: >
  "Linux uses the tools' official curl|bash install scripts (tflint/tfsec/trivy)
  rather than vendoring binaries — the documented path, at the cost of remote-script
  pipes. terraform-docs has no install script, so it's a pinned release tarball
  (bump TERRAFORM_DOCS_VERSION to update). macOS installs defensively via brew even
  though the Brewfile already declares these, so the topic is runnable standalone."
self_review:
  consistency: "infra/install.sh mirrors the docker/databases per-OS branch shape; Brewfile sections match existing grouping; packer added to the existing HashiCorp apt helper rather than a new path."
  error_paths: "set -e; pipx-missing and brew-missing and unsupported-OS all exit 1; mktemp dir cleaned for terraform-docs."
  security: "Three official install scripts piped to bash/sh (flagged); terraform-docs tarball over https to a mktemp dir then installed with mode 0755; trivy script pinned to /usr/local/bin."
  api: "New topic installer; Brewfile additions; ubuntu.sh hashicorp helper gains packer. Not yet called by bin/dot (PR 3)."
confidence: medium
reviewer_attention:
  - "infra/install.sh:48-52 — three curl|bash official installers (tflint/tfsec/trivy) on Linux"
  - "infra/install.sh:13 — terraform-docs pinned at 0.19.0 (no install script); confirm/bump"
  - "homebrew/Brewfile:7,68 — tflint via terraform-linters/tap; brew bundle taps then installs"
